---
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { product, publicRoutes } from '@content/site';

const page = publicRoutes.find((route) => route.path === '/terms')!;
---

<BaseLayout title={page.title} description={page.description}>
  <section class="page-shell">
    <p class="eyebrow">Effective May 30, 2026</p>
    <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
    <p>
      These Terms govern access to Clarity, including the public website, mobile app, account
      connection features, Rex assistant, waitlist, contact forms, and support paths.
    </p>
    <p>
      By using Clarity, you agree to use the product responsibly and understand that Clarity is not
      a regulated financial, legal, tax, accounting, banking, lending, brokerage, or investment
      advisory service.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="service-heading">
    <div class="section__header">
      <p class="eyebrow">The service</p>
      <h2 id="service-heading">Clarity helps organize personal financial context.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="panel">
      <p>
        Clarity provides tools for reviewing spending, budgets, goals, financial context,
        assistant conversations, memory, and related planning workflows. Rex is the AI assistant
        inside Clarity. Rex may help summarize information, explain options, and organize context,
        but you remain responsible for your own decisions.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="eligibility-heading">
    <div class="section__header">
      <p class="eyebrow">Eligibility and accounts</p>
      <h2 id="eligibility-heading">Use your own information and keep account access secure.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="card-grid">
      <article class="panel">
        <h3>Personal use</h3>
        <p>
          Clarity is intended for personal use by people who can form a binding agreement and use
          the product in compliance with applicable laws.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="panel">
        <h3>Accurate information</h3>
        <p>
          You are responsible for the information you provide, upload, connect, or ask Clarity to
          process.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="panel">
        <h3>Account security</h3>
        <p>
          Keep your sign-in credentials secure. Do not share access, submit bank passwords through
          public forms, or use Clarity to access accounts you are not authorized to use.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="financial-heading">
    <div class="section__header">
      <p class="eyebrow">Financial boundaries</p>
      <h2 id="financial-heading">Clarity and Rex do not replace professional advice.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="panel">
      <p>
        Clarity may provide summaries, categories, forecasts, suggestions, or assistant responses
        based on available context. These outputs may be incomplete, delayed, inaccurate, or not
        appropriate for your situation. You should review information carefully and consult
        qualified professionals for investment, tax, legal, accounting, credit, insurance, or other
        regulated advice.
      </p>
      <p>
        Clarity and Rex do not move money, pay bills, open accounts, apply for credit, file taxes,
        make purchases, or take external financial actions for you.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="plaid-heading">
    <div class="section__header">
      <p class="eyebrow">Connected accounts</p>
      <h2 id="plaid-heading">Account connections depend on user permission and providers.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="panel">
      <p>
        Clarity is designed to use user-authorized account-connection providers such as Plaid.
        Available data may depend on your financial institution, connection provider, permissions,
        account type, and product configuration. Clarity does not guarantee continuous access,
        immediate balance updates, exhaustive transaction coverage, or error-free categorization.
      </p>
      <p>
        You may be able to disconnect accounts where supported, and you can request help through
        the published <a href="/data-deletion">Data Deletion</a> or <a href="/contact">Contact</a>
        paths.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="acceptable-heading">
    <div class="section__header">
      <p class="eyebrow">Acceptable use</p>
      <h2 id="acceptable-heading">Use Clarity lawfully and safely.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="panel">
      <ul>
        <li>Do not use Clarity to access accounts or data you are not authorized to access.</li>
        <li>Do not submit malware, abusive content, secrets, credentials, or sensitive documents through public forms.</li>
        <li>Do not attempt to disrupt, scrape, reverse engineer, overload, or bypass product controls.</li>
        <li>Do not use Clarity to commit fraud, evade law, impersonate others, or make prohibited financial decisions.</li>
        <li>Do not rely on Rex outputs as the only basis for important financial, legal, tax, credit, health, or safety decisions.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="availability-heading">
    <div class="section__header">
      <p class="eyebrow">Availability and changes</p>
      <h2 id="availability-heading">Clarity may change as the product develops.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="panel">
      <p>
        Clarity may be modified, paused, limited, or discontinued. Features may depend on third
        parties, financial institutions, internet access, AI providers, speech providers, hosting
        providers, account-connection providers, and user permissions.
      </p>
      <p>
        We may update these Terms from time to time. Continued use of Clarity after changes means
        you accept the updated Terms.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="warranty-heading">
    <div class="section__header">
      <p class="eyebrow">Important limitations</p>
      <h2 id="warranty-heading">Use Clarity with judgment.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="panel">
      <p>
        Clarity is provided on an as-available basis. We do not promise that the product will be
        uninterrupted, error-free, perfectly secure, or suitable for every purpose. To the maximum
        extent permitted by law, Clarity is not responsible for decisions you make based on
        summaries, categories, predictions, assistant responses, or third-party data availability.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="contact-heading">
    <div class="section__header">
      <p class="eyebrow">Questions</p>
      <h2 id="contact-heading">Contact Clarity through the published support path.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="hero__actions">
      <a class="button button--secondary" href="/privacy">Privacy</a>
      <a class="button button--secondary" href="/security">Security</a>
      <a class="button button--secondary" href="/data-deletion">Data Deletion</a>
      <a class="button" href={`mailto:${product.supportEmail}`}>Email support</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
